00:01:35.563 --> 00:01:40.443
A hundred megawatt data center can drink about 2.5 billion liters of water a year.

00:01:40.943 --> 00:01:44.903
Data center knowledge reports, roughly what 5,000 or more homes use.

00:01:45.423 --> 00:01:48.003
Almost all of that water is there to throw heat away.

00:01:48.003 --> 00:01:50.863
The common method is direct evaporative cooling.

00:01:51.563 --> 00:01:56.243
Air is pulled through wetted pads and the evaporation itself takes the heat out of the air stream.

00:01:56.823 --> 00:02:03.843
Most operators do not recycle it because the alternatives cost more to build and are harder to run than the current economics will pay for.

00:02:04.503 --> 00:02:07.423
Uptime Institute says there is no single water template.

00:02:07.963 --> 00:02:09.523
Each site has its own signature.

00:02:10.203 --> 00:02:16.763
Older halls often sit on open cooling towers and a new hall can be designed to use little water or none for cooling.

